  "trustHomeMeaning": "Counts are satellite thermal anomalies from the last 24 hours, not confirmed wildfires. Some may be agricultural burns, industrial heat, or hot surfaces.",
  "trustHomeSource": "Data comes from NASA FIRMS (Fire Information for Resource Management System), combining VIIRS and MODIS satellite passes. The server fetches new data about every 30 minutes; satellite passes and NASA's processing time can delay a detection by a few hours.",
  "trustHomeInterpret": "Only a high-confidence detection above 30 MW FRP and 350 K is labelled Very Strong Heat Signal. All other points remain thermal anomalies.",
  "trustHomeAction": "Tap a detection for confidence, FRP, and limitations. If you see smoke or flames, follow official emergency guidance and report what you observe.",

  "trustMapMeaning": "Each marker is a satellite thermal anomaly, not a confirmed fire. Red means very strong heat signal; orange high anomaly; yellow nominal; gray low confidence.",
  "trustMapSource": "Fire data is sourced from NASA FIRMS (VIIRS and MODIS satellites).",
  "trustMapInterpret": "Clusters only mean multiple heat detections are close together. They do not by themselves confirm the cause or size of a fire.",
  "trustMapAction": "Tap a marker to review confidence and FRP. If you personally observe a fire, use Report and follow official emergency instructions.",

  "trustRiskMeaning": "The risk score (0-100) is an index combining temperature, humidity, wind and recent NASA fire detections in the region — it is not the probability of a fire and not a guarantee.",
  "trustRiskSource": "Weather data is pulled from live meteorological feeds; fire counts factor in recent NASA FIRMS detections for each region.",
  "trustRiskInterpret": "Compare your region's score to the Turkey average on the chart — a score significantly above average signals elevated local conditions worth monitoring.",
  "trustRiskAction": "If your region shows Critical or High risk, avoid open flames and report any smoke immediately. Switch to the \"My Location\" tab for a personalized breakdown.",

  "trustNewsMeaning": "Headlines are automatically filtered to keep only wildfire, disaster, and emergency-related coverage — unrelated political or sports stories are excluded.",
  "trustNewsSource": "Articles are aggregated from 9 established Turkish news outlets via their public RSS feeds, refreshed continuously throughout the day.",
  "trustNewsInterpret": "A \"Breaking\" badge means the article was published very recently — always check the publish time, as wildfire situations can change quickly.",
  "trustNewsAction": "Use the Translate button to read non-English articles, or tap \"Related Fires\" on a story to jump directly to that location on the map.",

  "trustAlertsMeaning": "Alerts notify you when a satellite detects a thermal anomaly within 50 km. They are automated, not verified incident reports.",
  "trustAlertsSource": "Background monitoring checks NASA FIRMS data on a schedule and compares new detections against your device's last known location on your phone. For regional alerts from our server, your location is stored rounded to about 1 km when you start automatic monitoring.",
  "trustAlertsInterpret": "Confidence describes confidence in a heat anomaly, not certainty that it is a fire. Check FRP and brightness together.",
  "trustAlertsAction": "Grant notification permission and start Auto Monitoring while using the app. Use \"Scan Now\" anytime to manually check your surroundings.",
